{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"f20c95931cf797eac1ffa9f3d81cfbed85fb16b758f16bc884759ac6c37e78df","digest":{"component_or_area":"ticket creation - duplicate warning system","key_entities":["src/rebar/_commands/composer.py","src/rebar/_commands/recent_creates.py","src/rebar/_commands/idea.py","src/rebar/_lib_writes.py","src/rebar/_mcp_writes.py","create_core","duplicate_create_warning","recent-creates.json","verify.suggest_duplicate_tickets","fcntl.flock","CreateResultOut.duplicate_warning"],"problem_keywords":["duplicate detection","create-time warning","same-title tickets","advisory surfacing","duplicate prevention"],"propositions":["Duplicate tickets are only detected after agents begin implementation because no same-title check runs at creation time, even when titles match exactly.","A rolling 600-second sidecar journal (recent-creates.json) with O(1) fcntl-locked reads/writes can detect same-normalized-title collisions without scanning the store or adding a title index.","The duplicate warning must be advisory-only and never block creation, surfaced on stderr (CLI), logger (library), and MCP result field after the write commits.","Concurrent creates must serialize on the journal lock so that simultaneous same-title tickets both observe each other's presence in the recency window.","The feature gates on the existing verify.suggest_duplicate_tickets config key; when off, zero journal overhead is imposed."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787706063794214001,"uuid":"54945013-ee92-41e2-a62b-bfe40fed0cb1"}